<title>USA: Unilever up on results, unit sales.</title>
<headline>Unilever up on results, unit sales.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) in Anglo-Dutch consumer products group Unilever NV rose on Friday, boosted by a rise in profits and the planned sale of its specialty chemicals units, traders said.</p>
<p>The ADRs were up 8-1/4 to 188-1/4 in late-afternoon trade. Volume was a moderate 191,000 shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Things are on the move and there is a lot of U.S. buying in the stock,&quot; said Andrew Melinek, head of ADR research and sales at NatWest Securities.</p>
<p>The company this week reported a 15 percent rise in annual profits, to $4.4 billion, and said it would sell its specialty chemicals units in a move expected to raise up to $8 billion.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
